'''Embajadores''' ({{Literally|ambassadors|}}; {{Langx|mxi|إِيمْبَاخَاذُورِيسْ|Ambaẖađóres}}) is a predominately residential [[Communes of Balisca|barrio]] located in the [[Expansión]] borough, within the [[Castejón Metropolis]].  

The area was first settled by [[W:Maroons|Maroons]] as ''Jago'' during the [[Colonial Balisca|Aragonese colonization of the archipelago]] in the 17th century. It received its current name in 1836, when delegates ("ambassadors") to the [[1836 Confederal Convention]] were lodged in the area (then outside of the limits of [[Commune of Castejón|Castejón]]). Historically sparsely populated, the establishment of the [[District of Castejón]] led to it transitioning into a fully urbanized district called an ''[[W:Arrabal|arrabal]]'' by the late-19th century. 

